## 2. Transaction Propagation

Transaction propagation defines how a method behaves when another transaction already exists.

| Propagation | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `REQUIRED` | Join the existing transaction or create a new one. |
| `REQUIRES_NEW` | Suspend the existing transaction and start a new one. |
| `SUPPORTS` | Join a transaction if one exists; otherwise run without one. |
| `MANDATORY` | Require an existing transaction. |
| `NOT_SUPPORTED` | Suspend the existing transaction and run without one. |
| `NEVER` | Fail if a transaction exists. |
| `NESTED` | Use a nested transaction or savepoint when supported. |

Example:

```java
@Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
public void saveStudent() {
    // Database operations
}
```

**Interview answer:** `REQUIRED` is the default propagation. It allows multiple methods to participate in the same transaction.

