## 5. Authentication vs Authorization

| Authentication | Authorization |
|---|---|
| Checks who you are. | Checks what you can do. |
| Validates credentials or tokens. | Checks roles, permissions, and resource access. |
| Example: Doctor logs in. | Example: Doctor accesses an authorized patient's results. |

Example authorization rule:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
public void deleteStudent(Long id) {
    // Delete student after required checks
}
```

Enable method security in the application:

```java
@Configuration
@EnableMethodSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {
}
```

Role checks alone may not be enough. Sensitive applications must also validate resource ownership and access policies.

