## 7. CI/CD Workflow

CI/CD automates the process of building, testing, and deploying software.

### Typical workflow

1. Developer pushes code to Git.
2. Jenkins or GitHub Actions starts the pipeline.
3. Maven builds the application.
4. Unit and integration tests run.
5. Code quality and security checks execute.
6. Docker builds the application image.
7. The image is pushed to a container registry.
8. The application is deployed to the target environment.
9. Health checks and monitoring verify the deployment.

### Common tools

| Purpose | Tools |
|---|---|
| Version control | Git |
| Build | Maven |
| CI/CD | Jenkins, GitHub Actions |
| Code quality | SonarQube |
| Containerization | Docker |
| Orchestration | Kubernetes |
| Monitoring | Prometheus, Grafana |
| Cloud | AWS |

**Interview answer:** CI/CD automates builds, testing, quality checks, image creation, and deployment. I would also use deployment approvals, health checks, and rollback mechanisms to reduce production risk.

Use the tools that match your actual project experience when answering interview questions.

